[Music]  one of the biggest news stories of this  tumultuous year was the demand for  police reform  massive demonstrations were seen in  cities all across the country including  here in las vegas  does metro need to be reformed and if so  in what ways  this week 8 news now is looking at the  progress metro has made in the past few  years and how far  it still needs to go the i-team's george  knapp starts it off  on the streets of las vegas as in other  major cities protesters demanded police  reform their anger fueled by flash  points  such as the death of george floyd at the  hands of police  across the nation long simmering anger  at police  began as peaceful protests but erupted  into something else  it did make me sick to my stomach that a  singular officer  could cause so much strife across the  world sheriff joe lombardo heads one of  the largest police agencies in the  country  one that has vast experience in managing  large rowdy crowds  but he and others were surprised by the  anger  aimed at metro officers it was  eye-opening for me because i remember  when i first hired  if an individual was standing there and  got in my face  and said the things to me that they were  saying to my officers  in today's day it'd be a different story  i would probably lose my cool i watch  them i've seen video of them standing  there  with the worst things in the world being  hurled at them i mean people telling  them what they're going to do to their  wife  and their children right people these  people don't know these officers  and i watch these officers stand there  stoic and do their job as professionals  they can be  video images make it clear the police  pushed back  assorted agitators tried to incite  further trouble  a police car was torched an officer was  shot in the head  three militia members were arrested for  allegedly plotting to unleash molotov  cocktails  during a black lives matter event none  of this erupted in a vacuum for decades  las vegas was known for its tough cops  who didn't hold back  as for race las vegas was nicknamed the  mississippi of the west  well into the 60s the predominantly  black neighborhood known as the west  side  was viewed by police as hostile  territory  into the 80s it was a concern  of police officers to have to even work  that area you know it was considered the  battleground  of las vegas and through time that's  changed  change has occurred within metro but how  can it be measured  and is it enough more on that in our  next report  george knapp 8 news now the i-team was  given access to training  testing and transparency programs and  documents to see how metro measures up  tonight at 11 a look at key events that  led to major  changes within the agency

